-- title:
--   Branches with independent tangents contract to distinct stalk primes
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$.
--
--   Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the subgroup `levelH q M'` $\cap\ \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}\big)$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the image under coefficientwise extension of scalars [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero, with Laurent series the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model: the pushout of the two maps of affine schemes obtained from the inclusions of `chartAlgFin`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `chartAlgInf`, the elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, into the corresponding algebra for $\{j, j^{-1}\}$; `toBase` is its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the element of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ obtained by transporting $\varpi$ along $\operatorname{Spec} A \to X$ and taking the germ at $z$; it is assumed that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin})$ mapping to $z$ under the canonical morphism `ιFin`. The hypothesis `hss` is a supersingularity condition at $y$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no point $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ other than $0$.
--
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain, $\sigma : A \to W$ a ring homomorphism with $\sigma\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal of $W$, and let $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and
--   $$f - \big(X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1\big) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   the subtracted term being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18). Put $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v - f\,u)$ with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S$. Write $\mathrm{toC} : \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{X,z}$ for the completion map and $\mathrm{germ}_y : \mathtt{chartAlgFin} \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the composite of the canonical identification of the global sections of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin})$ with `chartAlgFin`, the inverse of the comparison isomorphism for `ιFin` on the whole space, and the germ map at $z$ on the image open set.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW` has two parts. The first (constants) states that for every $a \in A$ the image under $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ of the germ at $z$ of $a$, taken along `toBase`, is $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma a))$. The second (linearised level action) states: for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — namely that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_1, g_1$ of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and all embeddings $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g_1 \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f_1 \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta = \begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q \\ q\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ — and every proof that $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin` into itself, if the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin` is congruent to the identity modulo the prime $y$, then there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_y$ with the action of $\tau$ on `chartAlgFin`; $\theta$ fixes every $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$, $w \in W$; for each index $j_0$, $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(X_{j_0})) - \mathrm{mk}_S\big(\sum_i C(M_{i j_0})X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0), \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$; $c^{q+1} - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$; $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c \equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c - 1$ does not lie in the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` consists of two clauses about level automorphisms, free of the above witness: first, every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps `chartAlgFin` into itself; second, if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, then the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin` is congruent to the identity modulo the prime $y$, i.e. $\tau a - a \in y$ for all $a$ in `chartAlgFin`.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the following implication. Assume there exist two distinct prime ideals $Q_1 \neq Q_2$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, both containing $\varpi_z$ and neither of them maximal. Then for all integers $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that, for each $i$, at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0), \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$ lies outside $P_i$, such that $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma\varpi)) \in P_i$, and such that $P_i$ contains an element $\mathrm{mk}_S\big(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h\big)$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and such that $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along the composite $\mathcal{O}_{X,z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{X,z} \xrightarrow{e} S$ are distinct ideals of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$.
--
--   This is the branch-separation step in the local analysis of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point in residue characteristic $q$: two formal branches of the Drinfeld local chart whose tangent directions are independent modulo $q$ lie on different components through $z$, granted that the stalk has at least two non-maximal primes over the uniformiser. It is used, in the auxiliary level-one frame with a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ and a diamond condition in place of a congruence at $q$, by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_quotient_of_mem_of_not_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk_quotient_of_mem_of_not_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd).
